    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151">

                <pb facs="0129" n="119" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg119"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultations 3/39: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chilean Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Rossetti</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Chairman of the Governing Board of the Pan
                        American Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hull</hi>)<anchor n="3" xml:id="d151-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]<anchor n="4" xml:id="d151-f2"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-09T20:05:00-04:00">December 9, 1941—8:05
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In the presence of the unjustified aggression of which the United States has been
                    the victim on the part of a non-American power and having in mind the contents
                    of Resolutions XV and XVII<anchor n="5" xml:id="d151-f3"/> approved at the
                    Havana Consultative Conference in the month of July, 1940, I beg Your Excellency
                    to consult the rest of the American Governments concerning the urgent
                    convocation of a Third Consultative Conference of the Ministers for Foreign
                    Affairs of the American Republics to <pb facs="0130" n="120" xml:id="pg120"/>
                    consider the situation produced and to adopt the most adequate means demanded by
                    the solidarity of our peoples and by the defense of the hemisphere.</p>
                <p>I take this opportunity to renew [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Juan B. Rossetti</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d151-f1" n="3" type="source" xml:id="d151-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted to the Department by the Director General of the Pan American Union
                    (Rowe) on December 10, 1941.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d151-f2" n="4" xml:id="d151-f2-content">
                <p>Translation supplied by the editors.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d151-f3" n="5" xml:id="d151-f3-content">
                <p>Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, August 24, 1940, pp.
                    136 and 137, respectively.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
